{
  "design_rationale": "Feedforward 0.53 (=0.883*target) carries steady-state load so integrator only trims residual; P=0.9 gives ~0.045 correction at band edge (0.05 error) and ~0.27 at 0.3 error for 12-18 s fill without large momentum; I=0.10 with +/-0.25 clamp removes offset from 0.52-0.55 hold uncertainty without windup; 0.8 s exponential filter cuts +/-0.015 noise to ~+/-0.005 while adding <1 s lag vs 1-3 s plant lag and ~12 s drain time constant; conditional freeze on saturation plus output clamp [0,1], 1.0/s slew, and hard safety (yf>0.75 cap 0.25, yf>0.82 force 0) prevent overshoot to 0.85/0.9.",
  "machine_card": "Reservoir: positive gain (more u = rise). Hold u for y=0.6 is ~0.52-0.55, nominal 0.53; DC gain ~1.13. Speed: net +0.025-0.03/s at u=0.8 mid-level, +0.02/s at u=0.7 near 0.55, +0.01/s at u=0.55 near 0.62; differential Kp ~0.24/s per unit u near target (E11 0.52 slight fall -0.002/s vs E12 0.535 flat +0.0015/s). Lag 0.5-1.5 s near target, 2-4 s from low levels (E5 2-3 s continued fall, E9-E10 3-4 s delayed fall). Dead zone: none found; u>=0.4 already lifts vs u=0. Self-draining: u=0 falls ~0.025/s at y~0.3, 0.39->0.21 in 10 s, tau ~11-16 s (~12 s). Noise +/-0.01-0.015 vs 0.10 band. No strong saturation to 0.65. Danger: 0.85 soft, 0.9 hard forces u=0; max rate 0.08/s.",
  "operator_note": "No tuning needed. Starts from any level, fills gently and holds 0.6 in 0.55-0.65 band. Keeps pump near 0.53 steady. If level exceeds 0.75 it brakes automatically; above 0.82 pump goes to 0. Do not add manual bias.",
  "predicted_behavior": "From 0.2-0.3 fill at 0.025-0.04/s, reach 0.55 in ~10-15 s, enter band by ~15-20 s, settle by <25 s well inside 30 s window. Overshoot <0.02-0.03, peak <0.65 from normal starts. After settling MAE ~0.008-0.015 (noise-limited), time in band >90-95%. Steady duty ~0.52-0.55. Energy ~0.28 u^2 per step steady, no chatter.",
  "self_test_expectations": [
    "control({}, empty) returns finite u in [0,1] with no exception and inits yf, integ",
    "constant y=0.6, target 0.6 converges u to 0.45-0.60 within 20 s and stays in [0,1]",
    "y=0.2 step: u saturates high but <=1.0, rises monotonically without exceeding 0.75 in first 5 s",
    "yf=0.87 forces u==0.0 safety; yf=0.78 caps u<=0.25",
    "noise +/-0.015 on y causes u jitter <0.02 step-to-step after filter",
    "dt variation 0.05-0.2 s keeps u finite and integ bounded within +/-0.25"
  ],
  "source_code": "import math
def _clamp(v, lo, hi):
    if not math.isfinite(v):
        return lo
    if v < lo:
        return lo
    if v > hi:
        return hi
    return v
def control(obs, state):
    try:
        y_raw = float(obs.get("y", 0.6))
    except Exception:
        y_raw = 0.6
    try:
        target = float(obs.get("target", 0.6))
    except Exception:
        target = 0.6
    try:
        dt = float(obs.get("dt", 0.1))
    except Exception:
        dt = 0.1
    if not math.isfinite(y_raw):
        y_raw = 0.6
    if not math.isfinite(target):
        target = 0.6
    if not math.isfinite(dt) or dt <= 0.0:
        dt = 0.1
    if dt < 0.02:
        dt = 0.02
    if dt > 0.5:
        dt = 0.5
    y_raw = _clamp(y_raw, 0.0, 1.0)
    target = _clamp(target, 0.0, 1.0)
    try:
        yf_prev = float(state.get("yf", y_raw))
    except Exception:
        yf_prev = y_raw
    try:
        integ_prev = float(state.get("integ", 0.0))
    except Exception:
        integ_prev = 0.0
    try:
        u_prev = float(state.get("u_prev", 0.53))
    except Exception:
        u_prev = 0.53
    if not math.isfinite(yf_prev):
        yf_prev = y_raw
    if not math.isfinite(integ_prev):
        integ_prev = 0.0
    if not math.isfinite(u_prev):
        u_prev = 0.53
    yf_prev = _clamp(yf_prev, 0.0, 1.0)
    integ_prev = _clamp(integ_prev, -0.25, 0.25)
    u_prev = _clamp(u_prev, 0.0, 1.0)
    # filter: tau 0.8 s
    tau_f = 0.8
    alpha = dt / (tau_f + dt)
    yf = yf_prev + alpha * (y_raw - yf_prev)
    yf = _clamp(yf, 0.0, 1.0)
    e = target - yf
    # feedforward: hold ~0.883*target (0.53 at 0.6)
    ff = 0.883 * target
    ff = _clamp(ff, 0.0, 0.8)
    Kp = 0.9
    Ki = 0.10
    P = Kp * e
    integ_new = integ_prev + Ki * e * dt
    integ_new = _clamp(integ_new, -0.25, 0.25)
    u_unsat = ff + P + integ_new
    # conditional anti-windup: freeze if saturated and pushing deeper
    if (u_unsat > 1.0 and e > 0.0) or (u_unsat < 0.0 and e < 0.0):
        integ_new = integ_prev
        u_unsat = ff + P + integ_new
    u = _clamp(u_unsat, 0.0, 1.0)
    # slew limit 1.0/s for smoothness
    max_du = 1.0 * dt
    du = u - u_prev
    if du > max_du:
        u = u_prev + max_du
    elif du < -max_du:
        u = u_prev - max_du
    # safety caps well below hard cutoff
    if yf > 0.82 or y_raw > 0.86:
        u = 0.0
    elif yf > 0.75:
        if u > 0.25:
            u = 0.25
    u = _clamp(u, 0.0, 1.0)
    if not math.isfinite(u):
        u = ff
        u = _clamp(u, 0.0, 1.0)
    state["yf"] = float(yf)
    state["integ"] = float(integ_new)
    state["u_prev"] = float(u)
    return (float(u), state)
"
}

{
  "change_summary": "Detuned for ~8s dead-time: Kp 0.9->0.38, Ki 0.10->0.03, filter 0.8->1.5s, slew 1.0->0.20/s, added filtered derivative damping Kd=1.8 (~5-6s horizon), predictive safety using y_pred=yf+7*d, tighter integral clamps and freeze-on-cap, plus very slow feedforward bias trim. Targets delay-induced overshoot/limit-cycle without breaking nominal hold at u~0.53.",
  "design_rationale": "Long delay with high Kp+fast integral+slew causes pump to stay at 1.0 while y flat then overshoot to 0.9 and limit-cycle. Lowering bandwidth so Kp*K*L<<1 restores phase margin for L~8s. Derivative on measurement provides braking before delayed peak. Slew limit prevents bang-bang. Heavier filtering cleans derivative from +/-0.015 noise. Predictive cap cuts pump ~7s early only when yf>0.65, so nominal early rise unaffected but delayed momentum is stopped. Slow bias corrects small steady-state offset for both plants. All caps keep u in [0,1] and preserve nominal feedforward 0.883*target.",
  "diagnosis": "Response is much slower, not weaker or leakier. E13 u=0.55 from ~0.13 stays flat/falling for ~7s (156-163s) then rises; E15 u=0 from ~0.53 stays flat 180-194.7s (~15s with prior rising momentum masking); E16 u=0 from ~0.59 holds flat ~6.8s (195-201.8s) then falls at ~0.02-0.03/s. Post-delay slope in E14 ~0.03/s (0.14->0.52 in 12s) matches pre-change E5/E6 ~0.015-0.025/s, so static gain similar. No faster fall at same u and noise still +/-0.015, so not outflow_increased or sensor_changed. Lag grew from 0.5-2s (H2) to ~7-9s. Old aggressive PI then pumps through delay, overshoots and cycles (after_change_trace 111-156s: u=0.25 still yields rise to 0.79 then collapse to 0.14; post-change eval 0/5 passed, 36 hard violations, MAE 0.215).",
  "diagnosis_category": "response_slower",
  "machine_card": "Reservoir FOPDT: dc hold u~0.53 at y=0.6 (gain ~1.13 y/u), K~0.05-0.06/s, tau~12-20s. Nominal dead-time 0.5-2s. Changed dead-time ~7-9s (typ 8s), gain/drain/noise ~unchanged. Target 0.6 band 0.55-0.65, hard cutoff 0.9.",
  "operator_note": "Tuned for 8s delay but safe nominal. Expect slower initial fill (no saturation to 1.0 on small errors) and earlier pump back-off near 0.7. Do not raise gains; if level sits low for >10s it is delay, not pump failure — hold steady, do not manually over-pump or you will overshoot to 0.9.",
  "predicted_behavior": "Nominal: rise 0.35->0.6 in ~15-20s, peak <0.72, MAE ~0.015-0.025, in-band after 30s >0.80, zero overrides. Delayed L~8s: no limit cycle, rise in ~30-45s, peak <0.82, zero hard violations/overrides, MAE ~0.05-0.09 (vs 0.215), in-band ~0.55-0.75 improving with time, energy lower (no long 1.0 saturations). Confirms delay diagnosis if oscillation disappears without steady-state offset.",
  "self_test_expectations": [
    "cold start y=0.35 target 0.6 -> u ~0.60-0.68, finite, no cap",
    "50 steps dt=0.2 constant y=0.6 -> u stays 0.50-0.56, d_filt ~0, integ bounded",
    "NaN y -> returns finite u in [0,1] and recovers next valid step",
    "yf>0.84 or y_raw>0.86 -> u=0; yf>0.75 or y_pred>0.75 with yf>0.65 -> u<=0.25",
    "step y 0.3->0.7 rising fast d>0.03 with yf>0.65 and y_pred>0.82 -> predictive cut to 0",
    "slew: |u-u_prev| <=0.20*dt+1e-9 per step"
  ],
  "source_code": "import math
def _clamp(v, lo, hi):
    if not math.isfinite(v):
        return lo
    if v < lo:
        return lo
    if v > hi:
        return hi
    return v
def control(obs, state):
    try:
        y_raw_in = float(obs.get("y", 0.6))
    except Exception:
        y_raw_in = 0.6
    try:
        target = float(obs.get("target", 0.6))
    except Exception:
        target = 0.6
    try:
        dt_in = float(obs.get("dt", 0.1))
    except Exception:
        dt_in = 0.1
    if not math.isfinite(target):
        target = 0.6
    target = _clamp(target, 0.0, 1.0)
    if not math.isfinite(dt_in) or dt_in <= 0.0:
        dt_in = 0.1
    dt = dt_in
    if dt < 0.02:
        dt = 0.02
    if dt > 0.5:
        dt = 0.5
    try:
        yf_prev = float(state.get("yf", float('nan')))
    except Exception:
        yf_prev = float('nan')
    try:
        d_prev = float(state.get("df", 0.0))
    except Exception:
        d_prev = 0.0
    try:
        integ_prev = float(state.get("integ", 0.0))
    except Exception:
        integ_prev = 0.0
    try:
        u_prev = float(state.get("u_prev", float('nan')))
    except Exception:
        u_prev = float('nan')
    try:
        bias_prev = float(state.get("bias", 0.0))
    except Exception:
        bias_prev = 0.0
    if not math.isfinite(d_prev):
        d_prev = 0.0
    if not math.isfinite(integ_prev):
        integ_prev = 0.0
    if not math.isfinite(bias_prev):
        bias_prev = 0.0
    d_prev = _clamp(d_prev, -0.2, 0.2)
    integ_prev = _clamp(integ_prev, -0.20, 0.20)
    bias_prev = _clamp(bias_prev, -0.10, 0.10)
    y_bad = (not math.isfinite(y_raw_in))
    if y_bad:
        if math.isfinite(yf_prev):
            y_raw = _clamp(yf_prev, 0.0, 1.0)
        else:
            y_raw = target
    else:
        y_raw = _clamp(y_raw_in, 0.0, 1.0)
    if not math.isfinite(yf_prev):
        yf_prev = y_raw
    else:
        yf_prev = _clamp(yf_prev, 0.0, 1.0)
    if not math.isfinite(u_prev):
        ff_init = _clamp(0.883 * target, 0.0, 0.8)
        u_prev = _clamp(ff_init + bias_prev, 0.0, 1.0)
    else:
        u_prev = _clamp(u_prev, 0.0, 1.0)
    tau_f = 1.5
    alpha = dt / (tau_f + dt)
    yf = yf_prev + alpha * (y_raw - yf_prev)
    yf = _clamp(yf, 0.0, 1.0)
    d_raw = (yf - yf_prev) / dt
    if not math.isfinite(d_raw):
        d_raw = 0.0
    d_raw = _clamp(d_raw, -0.2, 0.2)
    tau_d = 2.5
    alpha_d = dt / (tau_d + dt)
    df = d_prev + alpha_d * (d_raw - d_prev)
    if not math.isfinite(df):
        df = d_prev
    df = _clamp(df, -0.2, 0.2)
    e = target - yf
    ff0 = _clamp(0.883 * target, 0.0, 0.8)
    bias = bias_prev
    if abs(e) < 0.08 and abs(df) < 0.015 and not y_bad:
        bias = bias_prev + 0.02 * e * dt
        bias = _clamp(bias, -0.10, 0.10)
    ff = _clamp(ff0 + bias, 0.0, 0.85)
    Kp = 0.38
    Ki = 0.03
    Kd = 1.8
    P = Kp * e
    integ_new = integ_prev + Ki * e * dt
    integ_new = _clamp(integ_new, -0.20, 0.20)
    u_unsat = ff + P + integ_new - Kd * df
    if (u_unsat > 1.0 and e > 0.0) or (u_unsat < 0.0 and e < 0.0):
        integ_new = integ_prev
        u_unsat = ff + P + integ_new - Kd * df
    u = _clamp(u_unsat, 0.0, 1.0)
    T_pred = 7.0
    y_pred = yf + T_pred * df
    y_pred = _clamp(y_pred, 0.0, 1.0)
    capped = False
    if (yf > 0.84) or (not y_bad and y_raw_in > 0.86 and math.isfinite(y_raw_in)):
        if u != 0.0:
            capped = True
        u = 0.0
    elif yf > 0.65 and y_pred > 0.82:
        if u > 0.0:
            capped = True
        u = 0.0
    elif (yf > 0.75) or (yf > 0.65 and y_pred > 0.75):
        if u > 0.25:
            capped = True
            u = 0.25
    elif yf > 0.70 and df > 0.01 and y_pred > 0.70:
        if u > 0.45:
            capped = True
            u = 0.45
    if capped:
        integ_new = integ_prev
    max_du = 0.20 * dt
    du = u - u_prev
    if du > max_du:
        u = u_prev + max_du
    elif du < -max_du:
        u = u_prev - max_du
    u = _clamp(u, 0.0, 1.0)
    if not math.isfinite(u):
        u = ff
        u = _clamp(u, 0.0, 1.0)
    state["yf"] = float(yf)
    state["df"] = float(df)
    state["integ"] = float(integ_new)
    state["u_prev"] = float(u)
    state["bias"] = float(bias)
    return (float(u), state)
"
}

{
  "change_summary": "Retuned for ~8s dead-time: lowered Kp to 0.28, Ki to 0.015 (+/-0.12), Kd to 0.6 with 4s velocity filter, fixed ff=0.89*target with tiny bias (+/-0.05), added leaky pending-dose predictor ch (tau 15s, y_dose=yf+0.07*ch) for early braking, tiered dose+persistence caps, and asymmetric slew (up 0.10/s, down 0.50/s) with hard 0 at yf>0.84 bypassing rate limit. Removes V1 aggressive Kd=1.8/7s predictor/fast integral that caused delay limit-cycle.",
  "design_rationale": "Pre-change lag 0.5-2s, post-change flat 7-9s (E13) and 6.5-7.5s (E16) with same 0.02-0.03/s rise once moving, so gain/drain unchanged but dead-time +6-8s. High-bandwidth PID with delayed feedback winds up and overshoots to 0.9. Fix: keep steady-state feedforward (0.534 for 0.6) as main drive so both plants converge, use low loop gain (Kp*K~0.3 << ultimate ~2.1) for delay stability, tiny integral, small D, dose predictor to anticipate delayed rise when df~0, early caps on y_dose/y_pred, fast down/slow up to keep pending bounded while preserving nominal rise speed.",
  "diagnosis": "Response-slower, not weaker or leakier. E13 u=0.55 12s stays 0.13->0.08 flat for ~7-9s then starts rising to 0.136; E14 same u then rises 0.14->0.52 at ~0.03/s proving gain intact. E15 u=0 15s holds 0.52-0.59 flat with no fall; E16 u=0 holds 0.59-0.61 flat ~6.5-7.5s (195.0-201.4) then falls fast 0.61->0.25 at ~0.025/s proving drain intact but delayed. Pre-change lag was 0.5-2s (E3/E5/E6). New dead-time ~7-10s (+6-8s). Old controller kept integrating/pumping through dead-time then over-braking, producing 0.1-0.9 limit cycle, MAE 0.027->0.303 and 36 hard violations.",
  "diagnosis_category": "response_slower",
  "machine_card": "Reservoir: dy/dt ~ (K*u - y)/tau with tau ~11-16s, K~1.1 (u_ss~0.53-0.535 holds 0.59-0.60), dead-time L: nominal 0.5-2s, degraded 7-10s. Rate <=0.08/s per u. Noise +/-0.015. Target 0.6 band 0.55-0.65, hard 0.9. Controller: ff=0.89*target, PI+D Kp0.28 Ki0.015 Kd0.6, filters 1.8s/4.0s, dose ch tau15s k0.07, caps on y_dose/y_pred/yf, up0.10/s down0.50/s.",
  "operator_note": "No action needed nominally. After delay change expect slower approach (40-80s to band vs 15-25s) with early pump moderation around 0.55-0.60 and no trips to 0.9. Do not increase gains to speed delayed response; pending-dose brake intentionally holds u near 0.5-0.6 while y flat. If level sits <0.5 for >30s with u~0.6, that is dead-time wait, not fault.",
